\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The spacious firmament on high.
\par With all the blue ethereal sky,
\par And spangled heavens, a shinning frame,
\par Their great Original proclaim.
\par The unwearied sun, from day to day,
\par Doth his Creator's power display;
\par And publishes to every land
\par The work of an almighty hand.
\par \pard\fi720   
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Soon as the evening shades prevail,
\par The moon takes up the wondrous tale,
\par And nightly to the listening earth
\par Repeat the story of her birth:
\par While all the stars that round her burn
\par And all the planets in their turn,
\par Confirm the tiding as they roll, 
\par And spread the truth from pole to pole.
\par    \tab  
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. What though in solemn silence all
\par Move round this dark terrestrial ball;
\par What though no real voice nor sound
\par Amidst their radiant orbs be found:
\par In reason's ear they all rejoice
\par And utter forth a glorious voice,
\par For ever singing as they shine:
\par The hand that made us is divine!
\par                                      Amen. 
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

